=======
    if (nights >= 14) {
        // a fortnight or more: fifteen per cent off, rounded in the hirer's favour to the whole pound
        total -= Math.ceil((total * 15) / 100 / 100) * 100;
    } else if (nights >= LONG_HIRE_NIGHTS) {
        // a tenth off, rounded in the hirer's favour to the whole pound
        total -= Math.ceil(total / 10 / 100) * 100;
    }
>>>>>>> REPLACE
```

In `hireCharge`, hires of 14 nights or more now get 15 per cent off the same total, rounded up to the whole pound the same way as the tenth. Hires of 7 to 13 nights keep the tenth, and shorter ones still get no discount.

I wrote the 14 as a literal inside the function because I couldn't see how the constants at the top of the file are declared. You may want to pull it out into a named constant next to `LONG_HIRE_NIGHTS`.
